---
import "@fontsource/syne/400.css";
import "@fontsource/syne/600.css";
import "@fontsource/syne/700.css";
import "@fontsource/syne/800.css";
import "@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css";
import "@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/500.css";
import "@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/600.css";
import "../styles/landing.css";

const modes = [
  ["Quick", "One contained correction", "Direct workers, no GSD", "Deterministic + Conductor review"],
  ["Feature", "Scoped product change", "A few worktrees", "Loop 1 + integration when needed"],
  ["Project", "Multi-surface work", "Discuss, DAG, waves", "Loop 1, Loop 2, fresh review"],
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="BGSD — harness-agnostic verified GSD conductor. Parallel worktrees, real verification, main stays protected."
    />
    <title>BGSD | Git. Ship. Done. On steroids.</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="nav">
      <a class="brand" href="/">BGSD</a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="#pillars">Why BGSD</a>
        <a href="#workflow">Workflow</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/filippo-fonseca/better-gsd">GitHub</a>
        <a class="docs-link" href="/overview/">Docs</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="headline">
        <div class="hero-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Harness-agnostic · verified · main-protected</p>
            <h1 id="headline">Git. Ship. Done.<br />On steroids.</h1>
            <p class="lede">
              One session: the Conductor scopes a prompt, fans out parallel git-worktree
              agents that each run a full GSD batch, verifies every change through real
              computer use, merges onto a safe <code>next</code> branch, and keeps
              <code>main</code> protected behind a human-only merge.
            </p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn-primary" href="/overview/">Read the docs</a>
              <a class="btn-ghost" href="/models/">Models & paths →</a>
              <a class="btn-ghost" href="/quickstart/">Quickstart →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="banner-wrap">
            <img src="/banner.svg" alt="BGSD pipeline: scope, parallel GSD worktrees, verification, merge to next" width="640" height="230" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="pillars" class="pillars">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Why BGSD</p>
          <h2>Verified orchestration,<br />not vibes.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar-grid">
          <article class="pillar">
            <span class="num">01</span>
            <h3>Harness-agnostic</h3>
            <p>Launch from Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex. The conductor reads MD files and runs plain Node — wherever you start.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar">
            <span class="num">02</span>
            <h3>Real verification</h3>
            <p>Tests, typecheck, lint, build first. Fresh verifier agents gather semantic evidence when needed. The Conductor adjudicates.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar">
            <span class="num">03</span>
            <h3>Main protected</h3>
            <p>All work lands on <code>next</code> and ephemeral worktree branches. Only you merge <code>next → main</code>.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="contract" class="terminal-band">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">The contract</p>
          <h2>Conductor reasons.<br />Workers build & verify.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="split">
          <div class="terminal" aria-label="Example session command">
            <div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
            <code><span class="muted">$</span> node bgsd/scripts/conductor.mjs \
  <span class="purple">"build audit log"</span> <span class="green">--feature</span>

<span class="accent">conductor</span>  your live session model
<span class="green">routine</span>   Composer 2.5 Standard
<span class="green">hard</span>      Grok 4.5 base (reason required)
<span class="purple">verify</span>    deterministic → fresh evidence
<span class="muted">merge</span>     next only · main is human-only</code>
          </div>
          <div class="body-copy">
            <p>Your session model stays the Conductor and Advisor — BGSD never replaces it. Default workers route through Cursor Agent CLI; pass <code>--no-cursor</code> for Claude Code / Codex workers as an equal alternative.</p>
            <p>Fast variants and Auto are never silently selected. Doctor fails closed when setup is incomplete.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="workflow" class="modes">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Workflow depth</p>
          <h2>Same safety rules<br />at every scale.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="mode-table" role="table" aria-label="Quick feature project comparison">
          <div class="mode-head" role="row">
            <span>Mode</span><span>Use it for</span><span>Build</span><span>Evidence</span>
          </div>
          {modes.map(([mode, use, build, evidence]) => (
            <div role="row">
              <strong>{mode}</strong>
              <span>{use}</span>
              <span>{build}</span>
              <span>{evidence}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <span>BGSD</span>
      <span class="lock">🔒 main-protected</span>
      <span>Harness-agnostic GSD conductor</span>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
